A drone inspects seven checkpoints $S, A, B, C, D, E$ and $G$ joined by two-way corridors. The neighbours of each checkpoint, listed in alphabetical order, are:

| Checkpoint | $S$ | $A$ | $B$ | $C$ | $D$ | $E$ | $G$ |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| Neighbours | $A, D, E$ | $G, S$ | $C, D, E$ | $B$ | $B, E, S$ | $B, D, S$ | $A$ |

Depth-first graph search starts at $S$ and uses a stack as the frontier, initially containing only $S$. It repeats the following step:

- pop the top node $u$;
- if $u$ has already been expanded, discard it and continue;
- if $u = G$, stop (the goal test is applied when a node is popped);
- otherwise mark $u$ as expanded and push every neighbour of $u$ that has not been expanded, in alphabetical order (so the alphabetically last of them is pushed last and popped first).

Which one of the following lists the expanded nodes in the order in which they were expanded?

